// A picture as paint: it fills a window (background), the letters of a text and the outlines
// of shapes (stroke), by the same words as a shape's fill: as cover, fit, stretch, tile or
// center, with size for a tile and at to shift it. A text is cut out of the picture by its
// letters, and an outline by its thickness. Each picture sits in the box of the text or shape
// it paints, so cover fills that box.
window size 640 420 title "picture paint"
photo = load "landscape.png"
badge = load "sprite.png"

draw [
  background photo as cover
  no stroke
  rect at 20 20 size 600 160 fill white alpha 80
  font "Inter Bold" size 110
  text "rocinante" at 40 18 fill photo as cover
  font "Inter" size 26
  text "letters cut from a picture" at 44 138 fill photo as stretch
  rect at 20 200 size 600 200 fill white alpha 80
  no fill
  thickness 22
  stroke photo as cover
  rect at 50 230 size 220 140
  circle at 390 300 radius 62
  stroke badge as tile size 24
  arc at 390 300 size 170 170 from 200 to 340
  thickness 14
  stroke photo as stretch
  line from 480 240 to 600 360
]
